+# Meeting authority PR A: Neon access-origin foundation
+
+**Issue:** `2660c6a4-3e8d-4f4e-b3bb-eb61446c3c98`
+**Blocking prerequisite:** `59efc6dc-07a1-4b31-9942-ba2f1fcac8e1`
+**Canonical database decision:** Forge memory `9a05c237-f135-4c09-86e8-887d4fcef617`
+**Classification:** Critical - authorization and data migration
+**Stage:** PLAN revision; not approved, blocked on prerequisite
+**Base:** `origin/main@42e30d88bc516dc6472c9f1bb837bd694844aa47`
+
+## Outcome
+
+On one proven Neon physical database, establish a dormant meeting access-origin
+foundation without widening any read. Every meeting may link to one Product-
+Suite conversation, every escaping derivative has a nullable place to retain
+that origin later, and one server-side SQL statement resolves the authenticated
+caller through internal identity, active organization membership, active actor,
+and current conversation membership.
+
+Neon is the sole live database authority. Historical Supabase names, files,
+configuration, and comments are migration residue, not a supported topology.
+This plan creates no Supabase path and assigns no new hosted migration to
+Alembic. Issue `59ef...` must first prove the Neon topology and land the single
+canonical migration owner/order. PR A then consumes that landed result without
+adding a second journal or runner.
+
+## Prerequisite contract from `59ef...`
+
+PR A remains Forge-blocked until the prerequisite handoff provides and live
+verification confirms all of:
+
+1. one Neon project/database/schema topology for meeting, identity,
+   collaboration, memory, proposal, and work-item tables;
+2. the one supported migration root, runner, journal/revision rule, next
+   available migration identifier, deployment command, and fresh-clone path;
+3. `DATABASE_URL` provenance for both meeting and platform runtimes, with stale
+   Supabase defaults/adapters rejected in supported production configuration;
+4. the canonical identity/tenant tables and their key/constraint shapes;
+5. historical Alembic/Supabase files classified as immutable history or removed
+   adapters, never a second live migration authority.
+
+Before DEV, amend the placeholders below mechanically with the landed
+`canonical_migration_root`, `canonical_next_revision`, and exact deployment
+command from `59ef...`; re-run conflict and migration-order checks. If the
+prerequisite does not establish all five facts, PR A stays blocked rather than
+guessing.
+
+## Locked security contract
+
+- Active `conversation_memberships` is the sole MVP group grant. Existing
+  `reader|writer|admin`, `active|removed`, and conversation lifecycle values do
+  not change.
+- Authentication provider identity may map a verified subject to an internal
+  user; it is never a meeting grant. Request bodies, models, tools, connectors,
+  labels, emails, and legacy visibility cannot select caller, actor, tenant,
+  origin, or membership.
+- Durable, verified tenant and principal mappings resolve
+  `meeting_tenant_id -> platform_tenant_id` and then the complete
+  `(meeting_tenant_id, meeting_user_id) ->
+  (platform_tenant_id, platform_user_id)` pair. Equality, email matching, and
+  provider claims are forbidden shortcuts.
+- Same-tenant composite FKs protect every conversation origin. Positive
+  authorization is request-local and never an offline or cross-request cache.
+- Direct denials have one public `not_found` response. Search-style callers
+  receive an empty lane. Deterministic private reason codes are operator-only.
+- Database/migration mismatch, missing mapping/origin, inactive/revoked state,
+  ambiguous identity, and query failure deny.
+
+## Delivery split
+
+The earlier single-PR estimate was too broad. Deliver two sequential medium PRs
+under this child, both after `59ef...` merges:
+
+### PR A1 - Contract and response-shape freeze
+
+Freeze API/domain projections before adding columns, then lock the access-origin
+contract. No schema or authorization behavior changes.
+
+### PR A2 - Neon schema, backfill, authorization, and conformance
+
+Use only the prerequisite's canonical Neon migration plane. Add mapping/origin
+schema, perform owner-only meeting backfill, add the one-statement authorization
+primitive, and prove it on ephemeral Neon. No existing content call site uses
+the new primitive until PR B.
+
+A1 must merge before A2 branches. PR B still owns derivative propagation,
+memory visibility/enforcement, candidate UX/promotion, and existing read/action
+enforcement.
+
+## PR A1: contract and explicit response projections
+
+Extend `meetingCoreContract` in place with `accessAuthorityVersion: 1` and keys
+for the meeting origin, derivative origin, durable principal mapping, internal
+human actor ownership `identity.user`, current active membership, opaque denial,
+request-local evaluation, and explicit false grants for provider identity,
+participant labels, email matching, identifier equality, and legacy visibility.
+Do not duplicate roles or bump `conversationContract.authorityVersion`.
+
+Before any new DB column exists, replace wildcard output for the affected
+content models with named, versioned projection constants:
+
+| Projection | Current wildcard surfaces to replace | Public compatibility rule |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `MEETING_API_COLUMNS` | meeting `SELECT *`, update `RETURNING *`, search meeting-map selection, generic record serialization in `apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py` | exactly the current `Meeting` response fields; never `conversation_id` or mapping/audit fields |
+| `MEMORY_ROW_COLUMNS` | `RETURNING='*'`, memory detail/source/chain/list/update returns | exactly current `MemoryRow`; no `access_conversation_id` |
+| `PROPOSAL_ROW_COLUMNS` | create/list/get and route decision returns; proposal serializers | exactly current `ProposalRow`; no origin/source linkage columns |
+| `WORK_ITEM_ROW_COLUMNS` | work-item fetch/create/update returns | exactly current domain/API `WorkItem`; no origin/source linkage columns |
+| `WORK_ITEM_SNAPSHOT_FIELDS` | `to_jsonb(work_items)` in proposal create/apply/undo | only currently approved target fields; never new authority/provenance columns |
+
+Internal SQL may read authority columns only in A2's private repository/backfill;
+it cannot pass raw rows to a route or generic serializer. Projection tests
+assert exact keys on list/detail/create/update and proposal snapshot responses.
+This is API compatibility, not a new API version.
+
+## PR A2: exact Neon schema contract
+
+All DDL is one migration at:
+`<canonical_migration_root>/<canonical_next_revision>_meeting_authority_foundation.sql`.
+The root/revision are outputs of `59ef...`, not choices made by this blocked
+plan. There is no Alembic revision, second journal entry, search-path branch, or
+Supabase migration. The canonical schema model/type file established by
+`59ef...` is updated in the same PR.
+
+### Durable principal mapping
+
+Add `meeting_tenant_mappings`:
+
+| Column | Definition |
+| --- | --- |
+| `id` | UUID primary key, generated |
+| `meeting_tenant_id` | TEXT NOT NULL, unique source tenant |
+| `platform_tenant_id` | TEXT NOT NULL, FK to canonical tenant table |
+| `status` | `active|revoked`, NOT NULL |
+| `verification_method` | `admin_verified|migration_verified|product_sync`, NOT NULL |
+| `evidence_ref` | TEXT NOT NULL; opaque Product-Suite evidence ID |
+| `verified_by_actor_id` | UUID NOT NULL |
+| `verified_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL |
+| `revoked_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ NULL |
+| `created_at`,`updated_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL |
+
+It has a unique key `(meeting_tenant_id,platform_tenant_id)`, composite FK
+`(platform_tenant_id,verified_by_actor_id)` to collaboration actors, the active/
+revoked timestamp check, and an index `(platform_tenant_id,status)`.
+
+Add `meeting_principal_mappings`:
+
+| Column | Definition |
+| --- | --- |
+| `id` | UUID primary key, generated |
+| `meeting_tenant_id` | TEXT NOT NULL |
+| `meeting_user_id` | TEXT NOT NULL |
+| `platform_tenant_id` | TEXT NOT NULL, FK to canonical tenant table |
+| `platform_user_id` | TEXT NOT NULL, FK to canonical user table |
+| `status` | `active|revoked`, NOT NULL |
+| `verification_method` | `admin_verified|migration_verified|product_sync`, NOT NULL |
+| `evidence_ref` | TEXT NOT NULL; opaque Product-Suite evidence ID, not email/provider data |
+| `verified_by_actor_id` | UUID NOT NULL |
+| `verified_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL |
+| `revoked_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ NULL |
+| `created_at`,`updated_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL |
+
+Constraints/indexes:
+
+- unique source pair `(meeting_tenant_id, meeting_user_id)`;
+- composite FK `(meeting_tenant_id,platform_tenant_id)` to the exact tenant
+  mapping above, preventing users within one meeting tenant from mapping to
+  different platform tenants;
+- composite FK `(platform_tenant_id, verified_by_actor_id)` to
+  `collaboration_actors(tenant_id,id)` with `ON DELETE RESTRICT`;
+- check active implies `revoked_at IS NULL`, revoked implies non-null;
+- index `(platform_tenant_id, platform_user_id, status)`;
+- application/backfill additionally requires a current active organization
+  membership for the target pair. No environment JSON map is authoritative.
+
+Existing `MEETING_TENANT_MAP` remains untouched in A2 only for API compatibility,
+but neither the new primitive nor backfill reads it. Its retirement/replacement
+belongs to the `59ef...` reconciliation and PR B call-site cutover.
+
+### Origins
+
+| Table | Additive columns | Integrity |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `meetings` | `access_tenant_id TEXT NULL`, `conversation_id UUID NULL` | pair-nullability check; composite FK `(access_tenant_id, conversation_id)` to conversations; partial unique `(access_tenant_id,conversation_id)` |
+| `memories` | `access_conversation_id UUID NULL` | composite same-tenant FK; partial lookup index |
+| `knowledge_chunks` | same | composite same-tenant FK; partial lookup index |
+| `proposals` | `access_conversation_id UUID NULL`, `source_meeting_id TEXT NULL`, `source_action_item_id TEXT NULL` | composite same-tenant FK; partial lookup index |
+| `work_items` | same three columns | composite same-tenant FK; partial lookup index |
+| `meeting_promotions` | `meeting_id TEXT NULL`, `access_conversation_id UUID NULL` | composite same-tenant FK; partial lookup index |
+
+`meetings.access_tenant_id` and `meetings.conversation_id` are the only origin
+fields A2 backfills. They are both null or both non-null. Every derivative
+origin and source column remains NULL in A2. Do not add `conversation` to
+`memory_visibility`, alter its private/org check, classify legacy derivatives,
+or change reads. PR B owns atomic derivative propagation, quarantine enforcement,
+dedupe changes, and the memory conversation lane after all content call sites
+are caller-aware.
+
+## Verified owner-only meeting backfill
+
+The operator command lives in the canonical Neon-owned package selected by
+`59ef...` at `scripts/meeting-authority/backfill-meeting-origins.ts`, with tests
+beside the Neon DB contract tier. It accepts exactly `--database-url-env
+DATABASE_URL`, `--dry-run` (default) or `--apply`, and required
+`--report <absolute-path>`. It rejects non-Neon supported-production URLs using
+the topology validator landed by `59ef...`.
+
+For each meeting ordered by `(tenant_id,id)`:
+
+1. Require one active `meeting_tenant_mappings` row for the meeting tenant, one
+   active `meeting_principal_mappings` row for its exact tenant/user pair whose
+   platform tenant matches that tenant mapping, and one
+   current active organization membership for mapped platform user/tenant.
+2. Reuse one active human actor for the mapped internal user. Missing actor is
+   reported; read-side/backfill never provisions or guesses it.
+3. Reuse an exact active conversation with `legacy_source='meeting'`, matching
+   legacy ID/tenant and typed meeting subject, or insert using a fixed contract
+   UUIDv5 namespace over canonical platform tenant + meeting ID.
+4. Create an owner `admin` membership only when no membership exists. An existing
+   removed membership, lower/different role, disabled actor, archived
+   conversation, conflicting meeting link, legacy-reference conflict, or UUID
+   collision is quarantined. Never reactivate, unarchive, escalate, overwrite,
+   or delete.
+5. Set `meetings.access_tenant_id` and `meetings.conversation_id` together only
+   after all invariants succeed in one transaction. Unique constraints plus
+   compare-and-set make repeated and concurrent runs converge.
+
+The JSON report schema is fixed:
+`schemaVersion`, migration revision, run mode, started/completed timestamps,
+sorted counts, and sorted `{meetingId, tenantId, reasonCode}` entries. Allowed
+reason codes are `mapping_missing|mapping_revoked|mapping_ambiguous|
+organization_inactive|actor_missing|actor_disabled|conversation_archived|
+membership_removed|membership_role_conflict|origin_conflict|uuid_collision|
+database_error`. Never include content, title, labels, email, provider subject,
+transcript, summary, action text, proposal rationale, prompt, or credentials.
+Reports are operator artifacts outside the repository and are never committed.
+
+## One-statement caller authorization
+
+Add `authorizeCurrentMeetingCaller` in the collaboration repository. Input is a
+server-created verified caller identity `(authProvider, subject)`, requested
+tenant, conversation origin, and allowed roles. There is no `userId` or
+`actorId` input.
+
+One parameterized SQL statement uses CTEs/left joins over canonical
+`user_auth_identities -> organization_memberships -> collaboration_actors ->
+conversation_memberships -> conversations`. It requires exact provider/subject
+mapping, active organization membership, actor
+`human/identity.user/<internal user id>` not disabled, active conversation,
+active membership, same tenant throughout, and allowed role.
+
+The result is either allowed identifiers/role or public `{ok:false,
+reason:'not_found'}` plus one deterministic private code selected in this fixed
+precedence: `identity_unmapped`, `organization_inactive`, `actor_unavailable`,
+`origin_unavailable`, `membership_inactive`, `role_insufficient`,
+`database_unavailable`. No content/resource metadata is returned on denial.
+The primitive performs no provisioning, retry, cache, or logging. Routes may log
+only the private code plus policy version and opaque internal IDs; they never
+serialize it.
+
+## Executable ephemeral-Neon conformance
+
+Extend the existing `apps/platform-api/test/db-contract` harness only after
+`59ef...` makes its fresh-branch bootstrap use the canonical full Neon migration
+chain rather than identity stand-ins. Add a non-skipping command
+`bun run test:db-contract:meeting-authority` that exits nonzero unless
+`NEON_API_KEY` and `NEON_PROJECT_ID` are present. `NEON_PARENT_BRANCH_ID` may
+select the canonical parent; the harness creates and deletes an isolated branch
+and obtains its database URL itself.
+
+CI `.github/workflows/db-contract.yml` invokes this command for PR A2 with
+credentials scoped only to that step. Missing credentials, a skipped suite,
+zero executed tests, cleanup failure, timeout, or truncated evidence is
+INCOMPLETE/FAIL, never green.
+
+The real-DB fixture seeds distinct meeting and platform IDs for Alice
+(owner/admin), Bob (same platform tenant/no meeting membership), Carol (other
+tenant), and Dave (removed membership). It proves:
+
+- equality/email/provider spoofing never maps a principal;
+- cross-tenant FK rejection and identical public denial;
+- current allow, then committed membership removal, then deny on the next call;
+- two simultaneous backfills create one origin/membership and identical report
+  outcomes;
+- removed membership is not reactivated; archived conversation not unarchived;
+- UUID/legacy-reference collision quarantines with no partial mutation;
+- derivative columns and memory visibility remain unchanged/null;
+- response key snapshots are identical before/after migration;
+- branch teardown runs in `finally` and reports deletion evidence.
+
+## Deployment, rollback, and observability
+
+Order: merge/verify `59ef...`; merge A1; create a fresh A2 branch; apply its one
+canonical Neon migration; deploy dormant repository/backfill; dry-run/report;
+approve; apply; rerun dry-run for zero mutations; run required Neon conformance.
+There is no production feature flag in A because no read/write call site is
+activated.
+
+Rollback reverts application code and leaves additive Neon columns/mapping/
+authority rows intact. Never drop mappings/origins, restore a Supabase path,
+reactivate membership, unarchive conversations, or reinterpret legacy
+visibility. A later forward migration may repair data after review.
+
+Allowed telemetry: policy version, operation, allowed/denied, private reason,
+opaque tenant/actor/origin IDs, migration revision, report counts. Redact all
+auth claims, provider subjects, email, labels, meeting/derivative content,
+embeddings, prompts, tokens, and result counts visible to models/users.
+
+## Exact ownership and size
+
+PR A1 owns contract files plus the affected response-projection source/tests:
